# Wave W17-X (Route 210 — North): fog pine — a frosted fog pine, its crown gone pale under the murk, the frost carried in the tree’s own drawing (design: permanent fog banks rolling between frosted trees). On fog turf (ground baked in). Route 210 — North’s own tree — split from Route 210’s warm paddock pine by the frost entire and from the snow country’s pines ahead by kind: this frost is fog-borne, theirs is winter.
